@startuml
title Hospital Fixed-Asset Tracking System\nCommunication Flow Diagram

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam roundcorner 16
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho

actor "Authorized\nHospital User" as User

rectangle "RFID-Tagged\nHospital Asset" as Asset

package "Sensor Node Layer" {
    component "Registration Desk Node\nESP32 + UHF RFID Reader" as RegNode
    component "Checkpoint Node\nESP32 + UHF RFID Reader" as CheckpointNode
}

cloud "Hospital Wi-Fi /\nNetwork" as Network
cloud "MQTT Broker" as MQTT

package "Web Application Layer" {
    component "Registration App" as RegistrationApp
    component "Monitor App" as MonitorApp
}

package "Backend Layer" {
    component "FastAPI Backend" as Backend
    component "WebSocket Service" as WebSocket
    component "MQTT Processing Service" as MQTTService
}

database "PostgreSQL\nDatabase" as Database

' User interactions
User --> RegistrationApp : Node, asset, user,\nmovement and settings actions
RegistrationApp --> User : Forms, status,\nresults and warnings

User --> MonitorApp : Monitoring queries and\nmovement requests
MonitorApp --> User : Asset locations, node status,\nalerts and activity

' Physical RFID communication
Asset --> RegNode : UHF RFID signal\nRegistration scan
Asset --> CheckpointNode : UHF RFID signal\nAsset detection

' Sensor connectivity
RegNode --> Network : Wi-Fi connection
CheckpointNode --> Network : Wi-Fi connection

' MQTT messages from nodes
RegNode --> MQTT : MQTT publish\nRegistration scans\nHeartbeats\nAcknowledgements

CheckpointNode --> MQTT : MQTT publish\nRFID detections\nHeartbeats\nAcknowledgements

' MQTT broker to backend
MQTT --> MQTTService : MQTT delivery\nNode messages
MQTTService --> Backend : Validated scan,\ndetection and heartbeat data

' Commands from backend to nodes
Backend --> MQTTService : Blink or supported\nnode command
MQTTService --> MQTT : MQTT publish\nCommand message
MQTT --> RegNode : Deliver command
MQTT --> CheckpointNode : Deliver command

' Frontend API communication
RegistrationApp --> Backend : HTTPS / JSON\nAuthenticated requests
Backend --> RegistrationApp : HTTPS / JSON\nResponses and errors

MonitorApp --> Backend : HTTPS / JSON\nAuthenticated requests
Backend --> MonitorApp : HTTPS / JSON\nResponses and errors

' Database communication
Backend --> Database : SQLAlchemy / PostgreSQL\nCreate, read, update and delete
Database --> Backend : Stored records and\nquery results

' Live updates
Backend --> WebSocket : Asset, node, movement,\nalert and activity events
WebSocket --> RegistrationApp : Secure WebSocket\nLive updates
WebSocket --> MonitorApp : Secure WebSocket\nLive updates

note bottom of RegistrationApp
The browser applications do not
connect directly to the MQTT broker.
end note

note bottom of MQTTService
Incoming MQTT topics and payloads
are validated before database updates.
end note

@enduml